{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/62297-i-feel-nothing","id":62297,"title":"I Feel Nothing","path":["Home","Onyx Path","Additional Discussion","Off-Topic"],"posts":[{"date":"2014-01-31T10:38:24-08:00","id":62297,"title":"I Feel Nothing","content":"Hey, folks.<br /> <br /> Wasn't sure where else to discuss this sort of thing, so I figured here was as good a place as anywhere.<br /> <br /> The truth of the matter is that, right now, I don't feel much of anything. This is different from the depression I've grappled with for years, as that manifested as a powerful despair or sadness. This is different. <br /> <br /> First of all, some context.<br /> <br /> 2013 was a god awful year. It started out with some hardcore family problems, my sister moving in with me, my starting a new job as my manager that was making it worthwhile was retiring due to serious illness, then my sister blowing up and my having to take her back to my parents. All through it, I was moving through all my problems as best I could and just, well, surviving.<br /> <br /> Most recently, I've undone what could be called the nucleus of all my malaise. You see, I grew up with abusive parents who taught me that people in authority over you had the power to ruin your day on a whim if you did not perfectly meet their expectations. By extension, it taught me that <i>any</i> moment could ruin a day, or a month, or a life. I've learned, on an emotional level, that that is false now. A life is a scale, a balance between what you've accomplished and what you've failed at. As long as the balance is equal or weighed toward accomplishment, then things stay more or less on track.<br /> <br /> And all of that sounds good, right?<br /> <br /> Well ...<br /> <br /> As a corollary to the &quot;anything can be a ruiner&quot; thought, there was &quot;anything can be a succeeder.&quot; That is, if any one thing can bring an entire enterprise to ash, then, surely, there must be something that can create a new reality and dramatically improve one's circumstances. However, that's not really true either, as I said in the above section.<br /> <br /> So, now, there's just this lack of drive or meaning to what I want do do. I mean, if there's no the &quot;succeeder&quot; elements, what is there to strive for? If there's no &quot;ruiner&quot; elements, then what is there to overcome?<br /> <br /> Sorry for rambling. Back to your regularly scheduled programming.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/42-aranis","name":"Aranis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar42_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"229"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-31T10:57:35-08:00","id":62313,"title":"","content":"Sounds like you've discovered existentialism! Or is it absurdism? I never studied philosophy.<br /> <br /> It's a place that a lot of people end up, I think. In the absence of prescribed meaning from an outside source, there doesn't seem to be &quot;innate&quot; value to much of anything. So the question of what there is to strive for or to overcome doesn't really have a good answer. The answer is just whatever you feel like. Or you can decide that there isn't an answer, if you prefer.<br /> <br /> It's a bit of a mindscrew, yeah? It's liberating in a way to cast off the meanings that society/religion/family/etc. push on you, but discouraging to think that there isn't a universal answer. The best thing I can say to you, I think, is that it's important to realize that the meaning you ascribe to life isn't wrong or diminished just because you came up with it.<br /> <br /> Congratulations on resolving the damage your parents did to you, though. That's a good first step, and the void you're currently feeling should become less prominent as you fill it in with your own meanings and judgements.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/16-cielle","name":"Cielle","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar16_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"267"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-31T11:29:10-08:00","id":62338,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Cielle</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/62297-i-feel-nothing?p=62313#post62313\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Sounds like you've discovered existentialism! Or is it absurdism? I never studied philosophy.</div> </div> </div> </div>Both, really, as absurdism could be described as what happens when an existentialist and a nihilist have a baby.<br /> <br /> Anyway, there's usually 3 reactions to this state of mind:<br /> 1) Escaping existence, not recommended.<br /> 2) Create meaning thru whatever you choose (probably the healthiest option, religion is popular for this choice)<br /> 3) Accept the absurdity and continue to exist in spite (or to spite) it (can be unhealthy if taken to extremes, but so is everything)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>- If you must be ridiculous, I must ridicule you.<br /> - Those that can give up essential liberties in exchange for temporary safety deserve neither liberty nor safety. -- Benjamin Franklin</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/375-papa-bear","name":"Papa Bear","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar375_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1920"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-31T11:36:02-08:00","id":62341,"title":"","content":"That would be existential angst, yeah.<br /> <br /> Cielle is right if you ask me, define your purposes yourself and pursue them because you ascribe importance to them without concern for the opinions of others (well, except, maybe, the law...). You have to motivate yourself now, be your own engine, all the while keeping this feeling from usurping your thoughts and behavior. It gets easier over time.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2054-whim","name":"Whim","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"46"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-31T12:28:06-08:00","id":62373,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Cielle</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/62297-i-feel-nothing?p=62313#post62313\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Sounds like you've discovered existentialism! Or is it absurdism? I never studied philosophy.<br /> <br /> It's a place that a lot of people end up, I think. In the absence of prescribed meaning from an outside source, there doesn't seem to be &quot;innate&quot; value to much of anything. So the question of what there is to strive for or to overcome doesn't really have a good answer. The answer is just whatever you feel like. Or you can decide that there isn't an answer, if you prefer.<br /> <br /> It's a bit of a mindscrew, yeah? It's liberating in a way to cast off the meanings that society/religion/family/etc. push on you, but discouraging to think that there isn't a universal answer. The best thing I can say to you, I think, is that it's important to realize that the meaning you ascribe to life isn't wrong or diminished just because you came up with it.<br /> <br /> Congratulations on resolving the damage your parents did to you, though. That's a good first step, and the void you're currently feeling should become less prominent as you fill it in with your own meanings and judgements.</div> </div> </div> </div>Thanks for the congrats, and I'm certainly trying. I thought that's what I was doing before, but it was more like I was juts pushing back against the feeling of being able to be ruined at any moment.<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Papa Bear</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/62297-i-feel-nothing?p=62338#post62338\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Both, really, as absurdism could be described as what happens when an existentialist and a nihilist have a baby.<br /> <br /> Anyway, there's usually 3 reactions to this state of mind:<br /> 1) Escaping existence, not recommended.<br /> 2) Create meaning thru whatever you choose (probably the healthiest option, religion is popular for this choice)<br /> 3) Accept the absurdity and continue to exist in spite (or to spite) it (can be unhealthy if taken to extremes, but so is everything)</div> </div> </div> </div>Definitely wasn't considering 1, and 3 doesn't really feel possible for me.<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Whim</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/62297-i-feel-nothing?p=62341#post62341\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That would be existential angst, yeah.<br /> <br /> Cielle is right if you ask me, define your purposes yourself and pursue them because you ascribe importance to them without concern for the opinions of others (well, except, maybe, the law...). You have to motivate yourself now, be your own engine, all the while keeping this feeling from usurping your thoughts and behavior. It gets easier over time.</div> </div> </div> </div>A lot of it is just how <i>tired</i> I feel. I'm only 27. I shouldn't feel like I've already seen a million miles of hard road.<br /> <br /> But I do. And piling on top of that the idea that I have many more millions of miles of road ahead ...<br /> <br /> I just don't know if I can deal with that.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/42-aranis","name":"Aranis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar42_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"229"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-31T13:03:45-08:00","id":62413,"title":"","content":"27, feh.....<br /> <a href=\"http://www.imdb.com/name/nm0645949/?ref_=tt_trv_qu\" target=\"_blank\">Larry Kazamias</a>: Once a guy hits 18, it's all downhill.<br /> <a href=\"http://www.imdb.com/name/nm0001319/?ref_=tt_trv_qu\" target=\"_blank\">Shoop</a>: But it's a lovely ride.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>- If you must be ridiculous, I must ridicule you.<br /> - Those that can give up essential liberties in exchange for temporary safety deserve neither liberty nor safety. -- Benjamin Franklin</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/375-papa-bear","name":"Papa Bear","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar375_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1920"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-31T13:32:45-08:00","id":62433,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Papa Bear</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/62297-i-feel-nothing?p=62413#post62413\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">27, feh.....<br /> <a href=\"http://www.imdb.com/name/nm0645949/?ref_=tt_trv_qu\" target=\"_blank\">Larry Kazamias</a>: Once a guy hits 18, it's all downhill.<br /> <a href=\"http://www.imdb.com/name/nm0001319/?ref_=tt_trv_qu\" target=\"_blank\">Shoop</a>: But it's a lovely ride.</div> </div> </div> </div>Heh, fair enough.<br /> <br /> Also, as an update, the yawning pit of nothing that I was feeling has shifted into more standard depression. While that might not be something to celebrate in most circumstances, I can deal with depression.<br /> <br /> It's time for wine, friends, good food, and absorbing TV. I'm thinking Supernatural.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/42-aranis","name":"Aranis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar42_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"229"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-31T13:34:33-08:00","id":62434,"title":"","content":"I'm sorry your having trouble. Living with family is the closest thing to hell in my experience. One thing though I learned is if you are healthy cherish that because have broken body to go with a broken mind/spirit is infinitely worse. You may feel really low but it could get worse so much much worse. In that maybe you can find hope. If you are healthy you could always live anew even if you start from scratch. I hate feeling numb, maybe try watching a movie you know that will make you cry, the emotions should help make you feel human again. Being numb to long will scar you. I hated having to go through school like that. Find your emotions again, and try exercising if you can. When I wasn't feeling as unhealthy exercise was a good outlet, it was a way to feel like improving, and letting steam off. If you do it everyday, set a basic regiment of stuff like push-ups, squats, crunchers, you will notice improvement in morale as you improve in your routine. I recommend these ones because you can do them almost anywhere, when my life felt like a prison I did them. But know you have my sympathy. Seriously people shouldn't feel numb, it's awful. Do you have any friends nearby who you can trust? If you can open up to them maybe it can reignite your emotions.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/754-eldagusto","name":"Eldagusto","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar754_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-31T13:42:10-08:00","id":62439,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aranis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/62297-i-feel-nothing?p=62433#post62433\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It's time for wine, friends, good food, and absorbing TV. I'm thinking Supernatural.</div> </div> </div> </div>Just not season 6 of <b>Supernatural</b>....it would <i>increase </i>the depression. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>- If you must be ridiculous, I must ridicule you.<br /> - Those that can give up essential liberties in exchange for temporary safety deserve neither liberty nor safety. -- Benjamin Franklin</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/375-papa-bear","name":"Papa Bear","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar375_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1920"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-02T12:56:46-08:00","id":63558,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Eldagusto</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/62297-i-feel-nothing?p=62434#post62434\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm sorry your having trouble. Living with family is the closest thing to hell in my experience. One thing though I learned is if you are healthy cherish that because have broken body to go with a broken mind/spirit is infinitely worse. You may feel really low but it could get worse so much much worse. In that maybe you can find hope. If you are healthy you could always live anew even if you start from scratch. I hate feeling numb, maybe try watching a movie you know that will make you cry, the emotions should help make you feel human again. Being numb to long will scar you. I hated having to go through school like that. Find your emotions again, and try exercising if you can. When I wasn't feeling as unhealthy exercise was a good outlet, it was a way to feel like improving, and letting steam off. If you do it everyday, set a basic regiment of stuff like push-ups, squats, crunchers, you will notice improvement in morale as you improve in your routine. I recommend these ones because you can do them almost anywhere, when my life felt like a prison I did them. But know you have my sympathy. Seriously people shouldn't feel numb, it's awful. Do you have any friends nearby who you can trust? If you can open up to them maybe it can reignite your emotions.</div> </div> </div> </div>Thanks for your thoughts, Eldagusto.<br /> <br /> At least part of it was that I hadn't been taking very good care of myself lately. Really, that's something in general that I'm not very good at. In any case, I spent all of Saturday getting in some much-needed relaxation by playing Bayonetta, doing some freeform roleplaying, and watching Supernatural. It's just really hard for me to actually relax, and all that stress combined with the general void feeling didn't help anything.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Papa Bear</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/62297-i-feel-nothing?p=62439#post62439\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Just not season 6 of <b>Supernatural</b>....it would <i>increase </i>the depression. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>hah! Fair enough. I'm currently in season 2. <hr />Otherwise, status update.<br /> <br /> While I generally feel okay, my emotions are a big, confusing blob. There's still a pit of nothingness within, but that's mixed with anger, sadness, and anxiety that come and go, almost minute-by-minute. I've not felt this way before, and I can't say that I'm a fan.<br /> <br /> Though, in sum total, I am improving. So there's that.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/42-aranis","name":"Aranis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar42_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"229"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-02T14:00:26-08:00","id":63590,"title":"","content":"Have you considered about finding yourself a new hobby Aranis? Something which would let you focus on the hobby and relax instead of mulling over everyday problems even after work?<br /> I can't really suggest anything since I've no idea what you enjoy as past time but almost anything is better than just going home from work and watching telly.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1700-blue-fox","name":"Blue Fox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1700_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"191"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-02T14:18:52-08:00","id":63596,"title":"","content":"Aranis, I feel things will get better for you. I am 42, and can assure you time marches on. As to meaning, for those not given to religion (as I happen to be), I think that love can function as meaning. Caring for others is the best way to help one's self. I am not sure these observations (such as they are) will be of any help, but I wish you well with all my spirit.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/790-cire","name":"Cire","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"549"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-04T11:47:58-08:00","id":65026,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Blue Fox</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/62297-i-feel-nothing?p=63590#post63590\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Have you considered about finding yourself a new hobby Aranis? Something which would let you focus on the hobby and relax instead of mulling over everyday problems even after work?<br /> I can't really suggest anything since I've no idea what you enjoy as past time but almost anything is better than just going home from work and watching telly.</div> </div> </div> </div>Thanks for the thoughts, Blue Fox!<br /> <br /> I only recently realized that I hadn't been engaging much with my hobbies lately. A lot of that was due to the aforementioned one-and-only mentality, but it was also that, when I was growing up, my parents made me feel guilty for liking the things that I did. <br /> <br /> In any case, I've been playing more video games lately, and that's helped my mood tremendously.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Cire</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/62297-i-feel-nothing?p=63596#post63596\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Aranis, I feel things will get better for you. I am 42, and can assure you time marches on. As to meaning, for those not given to religion (as I happen to be), I think that love can function as meaning. Caring for others is the best way to help one's self. I am not sure these observations (such as they are) will be of any help, but I wish you well with all my spirit.</div> </div> </div> </div>Thanks for your thoughts, Cire.<br /> <br /> I'm still working on the meaning angle, but I derive the greatest meaning from my creative works. My main problem right now is doing that more regularly, as I have trouble making that pursuit a consistent one.<br /> <br /> And another part of it is that I don't want time to march on, in a way? I want things to be all right; I want things that have gone wrong to turn around and be good again.<br /> <br /> But that isn't the way the world works, is it?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/42-aranis","name":"Aranis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar42_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"229"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-04T13:31:45-08:00","id":65097,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Thanks for the thoughts, Blue Fox!<br /> <br /> I only recently realized that I hadn't been engaging much with my hobbies lately. A lot of that was due to the aforementioned one-and-only mentality, but it was also that, when I was growing up, my parents made me feel guilty for liking the things that I did.<br /> <br /> In any case, I've been playing more video games lately, and that's helped my mood tremendously. </div> </div> </div>Glad to hear your mood has improved and that you've found a good way to relax.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1700-blue-fox","name":"Blue Fox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1700_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"191"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-05T05:56:52-08:00","id":65605,"title":"","content":"I was in a similar situation, my family regularly insulted me for watching cartoons or enjoying any fiction that wasn't sci fi. Soak up dem hobbies to make you feel better.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/754-eldagusto","name":"Eldagusto","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar754_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-05T09:18:36-08:00","id":65743,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Blue Fox</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/62297-i-feel-nothing?p=65097#post65097\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Glad to hear your mood has improved and that you've found a good way to relax.</div> </div> </div> </div>Thanks. ^_^ Improving more today, too.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Eldagusto</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/62297-i-feel-nothing?p=65605#post65605\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I was in a similar situation, my family regularly insulted me for watching cartoons or enjoying any fiction that wasn't sci fi. Soak up dem hobbies to make you feel better.</div> </div> </div> </div>Thanks. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> I shall. It's something that I had forgotten how to do. Somehow.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/42-aranis","name":"Aranis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar42_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"229"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-05T17:01:08-08:00","id":66084,"title":"","content":"Aranis: I know what you mean. The swiftness with which time races by is appaling. We can but try to make our time count. Wait! I should have come up with a more cheerful way to say that.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/790-cire","name":"Cire","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"549"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-05T20:42:36-08:00","id":66231,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Cire</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/62297-i-feel-nothing?p=66084#post66084\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Aranis: I know what you mean. The swiftness with which time races by is appaling. We can but try to make our time count. Wait! I should have come up with a more cheerful way to say that.</div> </div> </div> </div>heh, no worries.<br /> <br /> And something that I've found is that you have to achieve a balance between fun things and achievement things. If you focus only on achievement things, then, interestingly, you don't achieve them. If you balance them with fun, though, staying focused and working is a lot easier.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/42-aranis","name":"Aranis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar42_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"229"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-05T21:17:33-08:00","id":66242,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Eldagusto</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/62297-i-feel-nothing?p=65605#post65605\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I was in a similar situation, my family regularly insulted me for watching cartoons or enjoying any fiction that wasn't sci fi. Soak up dem hobbies to make you feel better.</div> </div> </div> </div>... I just realized what you said there.<br /> <br /> Seriously? People that consider watching Westerns or Xena less appropriate than sci-fi?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Odd_Canuck is not a topical medication or food product and is not to be taken internally or seriously.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/31-odd_canuck","name":"Odd_Canuck","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar31_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1474"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-06T06:34:27-08:00","id":66438,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Odd_Canuck</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/62297-i-feel-nothing?p=66242#post66242\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">... I just realized what you said there.<br /> <br /> Seriously? People that consider watching Westerns or Xena less appropriate than sci-fi?</div> </div> </div> </div>Eldagusto can feel free to correct me, but my experience is that people who are going to be mean are going to use any excuse that they can find to be mean. If they can't find a reason, then they'll make one.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/42-aranis","name":"Aranis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar42_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"229"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-06T23:06:09-08:00","id":67006,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aranis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/62297-i-feel-nothing#post62297\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So, now, there's just this lack of drive or meaning to what I want do do. I mean, if there's no the &quot;succeeder&quot; elements, what is there to strive for? If there's no &quot;ruiner&quot; elements, then what is there to overcome?</div> </div> </div> </div>Would it really be so bad if the answer to all of those is &quot;nothing?&quot; Why not take a moment to rest from the <i>need</i> for something to do or accomplish or overcome?<br /> <br /> One of the great discoveries of life is that there is no inherent meaning to it other than what we make of it. I know that sounds depressing to a lot of people, but to me it's actually kind of freeing. None of what happens to you actually has to make you feel shitty because none of it is actually shitty or awesome or anything, it just <i>is</i>.<br /> <br /> You can't control what the world throws at you, but you <i>can</i> control the attitude you take toward it all, and in the end that's <i>everything</i>.<br /> <br /> So just maybe take a rest from trying to find meaning. That can get so <i>tiring</i> after all. Just take everything as it comes at you without judging <i>this is good</i> or <i>that is bad</i> and after awhile of just observing life as it is maybe you'll start to see some sort of pattern or meaning develop organically. It's <i>exactly</i> like taking in art or music, in my opinion. Reality is this wonderfully complex piece of music full of both pain and pleasure. Don't let other people's opinions, or your own preconceptions, get in the way of just <i>listening</i> to the rhythm. Open your mind and really appreciate all that life has to offer.<br /> <br /> I find that the more you pay attention and stay conscious to life, the more you learn to dance along with its hidden music. Whatever it throws your way, whether it's pleasure or pain, you dance along with it like an old partner instead of stumbling.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/avatar/20th%20Anniversary/2013~Mage%20The%20Ascension/img.php?h=120&amp;w=120&amp;img=1~M20.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1018-ophidimancer","name":"Ophidimancer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1018_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"596"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-08T10:29:33-08:00","id":67967,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ophidimancer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/62297-i-feel-nothing?p=67006#post67006\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Would it really be so bad if the answer to all of those is &quot;nothing?&quot; Why not take a moment to rest from the <i>need</i> for something to do or accomplish or overcome?<br /> <br /> One of the great discoveries of life is that there is no inherent meaning to it other than what we make of it. I know that sounds depressing to a lot of people, but to me it's actually kind of freeing. None of what happens to you actually has to make you feel shitty because none of it is actually shitty or awesome or anything, it just <i>is</i>.<br /> <br /> You can't control what the world throws at you, but you <i>can</i> control the attitude you take toward it all, and in the end that's <i>everything</i>.<br /> <br /> So just maybe take a rest from trying to find meaning. That can get so <i>tiring</i> after all. Just take everything as it comes at you without judging <i>this is good</i> or <i>that is bad</i> and after awhile of just observing life as it is maybe you'll start to see some sort of pattern or meaning develop organically. It's <i>exactly</i> like taking in art or music, in my opinion. Reality is this wonderfully complex piece of music full of both pain and pleasure. Don't let other people's opinions, or your own preconceptions, get in the way of just <i>listening</i> to the rhythm. Open your mind and really appreciate all that life has to offer.<br /> <br /> I find that the more you pay attention and stay conscious to life, the more you learn to dance along with its hidden music. Whatever it throws your way, whether it's pleasure or pain, you dance along with it like an old partner instead of stumbling.</div> </div> </div> </div>You make some really good points, Ophidimancer, and thanks for your thoughts! <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> The main reason that I think about these things is that I'm pretty darn unhappy with my life. I'm lonely -- both on the friendship and romantic fronts, I feel like I've not gotten anywhere with things that really matter to me, my family is a total failure that got confirmed when my little sister's behavior imploded despite my having literally rearranged my life so that she could live with me, and ...<br /> <br /> I'm just sick of it. I'm tired of being unhappy all the time. I'm tired of struggling to just get my hands on table scraps. Sometimes, I can put on a brave face and say to myself that I can climb up from the bottom and build something new ... But I've already done that. Many times. And I just don't want to any more.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/42-aranis","name":"Aranis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar42_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"229"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-09T10:46:45-08:00","id":68510,"title":"","content":"&lt;Professor Farnsworth voice&gt; Good news, everyone! &lt;/voice&gt;<br /> <br /> No, seriously, I do have some good news. The short version is that I'm fully through this issue.<br /> <br /> The longer version goes like this.<br /> <br /> While I had begun the initial breakdown of this particular knot in my psyche, the knot was something of nucleus. A hundred strands of sadness and disappointment and regret were tied into that knot so that when I begun slicing through it, all those strands were allowed to fly free. Consequently, my mood went into the toilet as I was overwhelmed with all kinds of negative emotions. <br /> <br /> As of last night, though, I actually got the biggest strand and traced it back to its source. The main reason that I was having such tremendous difficulty processing all this was that the succeeder/ruiner idea was something that was intimately bound to my parents. It was the first thing that they had taught me, and on a very deep level, i wanted that lesson to be true so that we could have a real chance of being a family ... even though that ship sailed long ago. <br /> <br /> With that desire resolved, the rest of the strands just started unraveling one by one. The desire to still be in a family through the first lesson I had learned was the sealant around each strand of rope, and without the sealant, then the ropes just flew apart.<br /> <br /> Where does that leave me?<br /> <br /> Well ...<br /> <br /> I don't feel so exhausted, now. I can start working toward the things that I want, and I can finally move past those various issues that have been tying me down over the year. All those issues that were, in fact, made possible by the very first issue I can remember having.<br /> <br /> So a brighter day awaits!<br /> <br /> In any case, I just wanted to say thanks to everyone offering your thoughts; they really did help. They helped me feel like a new man, and I can't wait to get started on this new chapter in my life.<br /> <br /> tl;dr -- I'm mostly better now; thanks for all your guys' help! <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/42-aranis","name":"Aranis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar42_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"229"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}